abstract: >-
  WITHDRAWN LOCAL RELEASE CANDIDATE. FLARE-24 and BC-POT-R investigate US
  domestic flight disruption probabilities and airport-boundary context.
  A later audit found that prior-operating-day histories did not establish
  flight-specific T-24 availability and that the legacy packaged smoke reversed
  cancellation and conditional-delay arguments. Historical scores and negative
  results are preserved as retrospective proxy evidence, not corrected forecast
  performance. New timestamp-validated experiments are required. The 2025 cohort
  is development-informed. The 2026 confirmation dataset was not opened, but
  incidental aggregate search exposure is recorded in the later source
  investigation. Corrected real-data training stopped at the evidence gate.
